            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0243" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23713: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-24T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 25—1:23
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>134. Telegram from vice consul of Great Britain in Tuxpam to his Legation here
                    declares serious conditions there and property interests of Americans should be
                    protected. Mexican authorities are said to be contemplating complete embargo
                    upon harbor of that city. Dawson sends no reports from Tampico to Embassy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
